  "transcript": [
    {
      "start": 1.3,
      "end": 16.3,
      "text": "Gary Moore, we have some good classic cuts by Styx and Yes and other people in the Friday Night Connection. New releases by Spider, Oz, Camel, Taipan, Baby Taco and Headpins. In other words, gotta be good, starting with this classic.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 16.3,
      "end": 29.5,
      "text": "we'll have some of that any day of the week any hour of the day that's a track from an album which",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.5,
      "end": 175.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 180.0,
      "end": 653.79,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 653.79,
      "end": 658.59,
      "text": "is just out on the solid gold record label they are called head pins the track was called don't",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 658.59,
      "end": 663.75,
      "text": "stand in the line of fire the album is called line of fire they're appearing they're fitting",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 663.75,
      "end": 672.33,
      "text": "with white snake on sunday night and i'm looking forward to seeing them before that you heard crazy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 672.33,
      "end": 679.7,
      "text": "train by ozzy osbourne from the album blizzard of oz ozzy osbourne track was requested by simbry",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 679.7,
      "end": 681.76,
      "text": "Cooper of Leamington Spa in",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 681.76,
      "end": 683.82,
      "text": "Warwickshire for a good friend of hers by the name of",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 683.82,
      "end": 685.72,
      "text": "Pete Briscoe, who's recovering",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 685.72,
      "end": 687.8,
      "text": "from a motorcycle accident. Wish him a speedy",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 687.8,
      "end": 689.76,
      "text": "recovery, and I do, and send him all",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 689.76,
      "end": 691.88,
      "text": "Simbry's love, and I do that as well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 692.04,
      "end": 693.52,
      "text": "Also say hello to all the students",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 693.52,
      "end": 695.64,
      "text": "at Kennington High, especially",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 695.64,
      "end": 697.8,
      "text": "Yvonne and Kaz and Penny",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 697.8,
      "end": 699.76,
      "text": "and Rach and Wendy and Michelle.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 700.42,
      "end": 701.82,
      "text": "Thank them very much for pulling me",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 701.82,
      "end": 703.88,
      "text": "through some bad parts over the past",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 703.88,
      "end": 705.52,
      "text": "year, says Simbry.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 706.82,
      "end": 708.32,
      "text": "14 minutes after 10, the Friday",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 708.32,
      "end": 714.06,
      "text": "rock show bbc radio one this is something from our session by palace it is called shock treatment",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 714.06,
      "end": 725.46,
      "text": "it's a four track 12 incher by taipan t-a-i-p-a-n it's out of a bullet record label in this country",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1203.08,
      "end": 1207.86,
      "text": "the track you heard rather was called lady and before that something from our session by palace",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1207.86,
      "end": 1213.74,
      "text": "they were in shock treatment hello to a gentleman by the name of clive preston",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1213.74,
      "end": 1220.16,
      "text": "father clive happy birthday from your missus that is your actually your mother's very missus at all",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1220.16,
      "end": 1226.16,
      "text": "from your mom sheila hello sheila as well happy 16th birthday to clive seems you're a man that's",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1226.16,
      "end": 1233.46,
      "text": "into all the top groups also i'm going to say hello to daz and belly and harry and keith and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1233.46,
      "end": 1241.86,
      "text": "glenn and mark from mrs freshton hi to all the cb mob in carlisle including newie also known as",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1241.86,
      "end": 1246.32,
      "text": "iron fist tell him that i miss him and i love him very much and i'm going to see him on sunday",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1246.32,
      "end": 1252.36,
      "text": "the first of april if everything goes well says carolyn close encounters also it says",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1252.36,
      "end": 1259.52,
      "text": "carolyn's in brampton in cumbria short shot to the point this is a little note from donna and",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1259.52,
      "end": 1265.2,
      "text": "from sandy from salta beck and they say please say hello to donna and sandy and tell sandy that",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1265.2,
      "end": 1275.4,
      "text": "donna loves him simple as that gary moore record album which is called rough justice the track",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1275.4,
      "end": 1902.5,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 1907.5,
      "end": 1912.67,
      "text": "title was midsummer morning they had the misfortune the other night of having to do a gig",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1912.67,
      "end": 1914.99,
      "text": "when all the transport facilities in London",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1914.99,
      "end": 1916.03,
      "text": "are totally closed down,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1916.09,
      "end": 1917.11,
      "text": "but they still had a good house",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1917.11,
      "end": 1918.43,
      "text": "and did very well on stage.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1920.14,
      "end": 1922.14,
      "text": "Prior to that, from our repeat session by Gary Moore,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1922.22,
      "end": 1924.08,
      "text": "the great track called Hold On To Love.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1926.44,
      "end": 1927.9,
      "text": "But Gary Moore was played for",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1927.9,
      "end": 1929.4,
      "text": "by a lady by the name of Manda,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1929.6,
      "end": 1930.54,
      "text": "Manda Taylor,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1930.9,
      "end": 1932.36,
      "text": "and also Graham,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1932.44,
      "end": 1933.58,
      "text": "when I say thank you very much",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1933.58,
      "end": 1934.82,
      "text": "for a lovely, lovely son.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1935.5,
      "end": 1936.88,
      "text": "Say also, says Graham,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1937.1,
      "end": 1940.04,
      "text": "hello to Flintstone and Nutmeg from us,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1940.18,
      "end": 1941.26,
      "text": "that being the Taylor family,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1941.74,
      "end": 1943.62,
      "text": "and Manda and the son.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 1943.62,
      "end": 1947.39,
      "text": "And Graham, indeed, you're absolutely right.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1947.49,
      "end": 1950.61,
      "text": "You will try to do your keep on trotting, boy.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1951.29,
      "end": 1955.31,
      "text": "Or should be north, but you keep it up as well.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1956.21,
      "end": 1960.45,
      "text": "25 minutes to 11, a little request card here for a fellow by the name of Tony",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1960.45,
      "end": 1964.05,
      "text": "and a mention for all the members of the Progressive Rock Society",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1964.05,
      "end": 1966.87,
      "text": "at Warwick University from Louise.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 1966.87,
      "end": 1975.0,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2007.66,
      "end": 2013.06,
      "text": "It's a track by a band called Baby Taku.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2013.06,
      "end": 2672.55,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 2672.55,
      "end": 2674.11,
      "text": "The album is called Firstborn.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2674.19,
      "end": 2676.61,
      "text": "The track was A-W-O-L, AWOL.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2676.61,
      "end": 2678.67,
      "text": "It's out on the Ultranoise record label.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2679.77,
      "end": 2681.77,
      "text": "Before that, a classic track by Styx.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2681.85,
      "end": 2683.49,
      "text": "It was called Sweet Madam Blue.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2683.89,
      "end": 2685.73,
      "text": "And I played it because I found a really old letter",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2685.73,
      "end": 2688.15,
      "text": "that goes back to the 3rd of November, 1983,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2688.37,
      "end": 2690.39,
      "text": "from a fellow who lives in Orpington in Kent.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2690.75,
      "end": 2692.39,
      "text": "That is Dave Pizzabaronte,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2692.69,
      "end": 2694.55,
      "text": "who wanted me to say hello to lots of his mates.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2695.03,
      "end": 2697.29,
      "text": "They are Wet'n'Cheese and Delirium, I think it is,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2697.61,
      "end": 2701.27,
      "text": "and Debut, and some gals by the name of Lorraine, Debbie, Mandy and Karen.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2701.75,
      "end": 2705.21,
      "text": "Also Martin, Tappy Edwards, Peter, Permanently High Clark,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2705.21,
      "end": 2707.57,
      "text": "and Craig Smokerscoff-Riddell.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2707.57,
      "end": 2713.85,
      "text": "and Sticks was for Ian Higgins, I think it is,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2713.93,
      "end": 2717.59,
      "text": "and Maria Mulligan of Balby and Doncaster",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2717.59,
      "end": 2719.55,
      "text": "and loads of other people as well.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2719.69,
      "end": 2722.81,
      "text": "Grum, Adolf, Daz, Bobby, Fretty, Mark, Smelly, Liddell",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2722.81,
      "end": 2726.13,
      "text": "and anybody else who knows Ian Higgins of Doncaster.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2727.77,
      "end": 2731.13,
      "text": "Sticks also requested for Pete Deamer,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2731.13,
      "end": 2732.91,
      "text": "I think it is, of Slough in Berkshire",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2732.91,
      "end": 2736.69,
      "text": "and for all his friends.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 2746.15,
      "end": 2748.39,
      "text": "Right, it is now 12 and a half minutes to 11.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2748.39,
      "end": 2751.15,
      "text": "This is the Friday Rock Show from BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2751.75,
      "end": 2753.57,
      "text": "Here's a long, long cut.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2753.75,
      "end": 2755.69,
      "text": "It's 13 minutes and 25 seconds long.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2755.83,
      "end": 2756.57,
      "text": "It's by Palace.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2756.77,
      "end": 2758.33,
      "text": "It's from our session by them.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 2758.81,
      "end": 2762.53,
      "text": "A medley, two songs, Rise and Fall and Heart Attack.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3590.0,
      "end": 3593.0,
      "text": "Our session by them, Rise and Fall and Heart Attack.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3595.44,
      "end": 3599.04,
      "text": "It's a minute and a half past 11 o'clock, the Friday Rock Show, BBC Radio 1.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3599.16,
      "end": 3600.68,
      "text": "Now it's time for the Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3600.78,
      "end": 3602.38,
      "text": "A fortnight ago, I played you these tracks.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3602.38,
      "end": 3606.58,
      "text": "I shot the sheriff from 461 Ocean Boulevard by Eric Clapton.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3606.96,
      "end": 3610.1,
      "text": "The Ocean from Houses of the Holy by Led Zeppelin.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3610.74,
      "end": 3619.08,
      "text": "And Ritual, Nusorm du Soleil, an excerpt thereof from the album by Yes Call Tales from the Topographic Oceans.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3620.1,
      "end": 3628.56,
      "text": "The answer was 461 Ocean Boulevard, The Ocean by Led Zeppelin, and Tales from the Topographic Oceans by Yes.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3628.98,
      "end": 3633.72,
      "text": "The winner is Annie Bickford of Gearswood Heathfield in East Sussex.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3633.72,
      "end": 3637.96,
      "text": "who wrote it on events wonderful at last i've been able to fathom out one of your infamous",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3637.96,
      "end": 3642.5,
      "text": "connections and i'm proud of myself despite your remarks to the effect that tonight's selection",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3642.5,
      "end": 3648.38,
      "text": "was not too difficult annie bigfoot congratulations 12 pound record token coming your way also a copy",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3648.38,
      "end": 3653.92,
      "text": "of the international encyclopedia of hard rock and heavy metal by tony jasper also a picture",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3653.92,
      "end": 3658.52,
      "text": "disc of barclay james harvest also a picture disc of heavy petting and also a picture this",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3658.52,
      "end": 3659.24,
      "text": "my spider.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3661.55,
      "end": 3662.97,
      "text": "Buy none, get them all free.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3663.82,
      "end": 3665.02,
      "text": "In the post, shortly.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3665.4,
      "end": 3667.6,
      "text": "Now Annie's put together her own Friday Night Connection.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3667.74,
      "end": 3669.84,
      "text": "It's in here somewhere. Three bits of music.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 3670.57,
      "end": 3671.45,
      "text": "Start concentrating.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3672.17,
      "end": 3672.53,
      "text": "Now.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 3672.99,
      "end": 3677.19,
      "text": "The Friday Night Connection of Annie Bickford.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4630.48,
      "end": 4632.56,
      "text": "Of Gearswood, Heathfield,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4632.78,
      "end": 4633.5,
      "text": "East Sussex.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4633.86,
      "end": 4636.52,
      "text": "Not a, I think, particularly difficult one,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4636.52,
      "end": 4638.8,
      "text": "Annie, but a magnificent choice",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4638.8,
      "end": 4641.62,
      "text": "of music. Okay, if you",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4641.62,
      "end": 4643.3,
      "text": "think you know where the connection is, it's in there somewhere.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4643.3,
      "end": 4645.48,
      "text": "in that little triptych.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4646.34,
      "end": 4647.48,
      "text": "Cut it down on a postcard,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4647.72,
      "end": 4648.38,
      "text": "back of an envelope,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4648.48,
      "end": 4649.78,
      "text": "any form of written communication",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4649.78,
      "end": 4651.1,
      "text": "you care to employ,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4651.28,
      "end": 4651.94,
      "text": "and send it to",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4651.94,
      "end": 4654.03,
      "text": "the Friday Rock Show,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4654.69,
      "end": 4656.03,
      "text": "the Friday Night Connection, actually,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4656.29,
      "end": 4657.33,
      "text": "and the Friday Rock Show,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4657.83,
      "end": 4658.87,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4659.39,
      "end": 4660.29,
      "text": "Broadcasting House,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4660.49,
      "end": 4660.79,
      "text": "London,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4661.07,
      "end": 4662.45,
      "text": "W1A4WW,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4662.93,
      "end": 4663.19,
      "text": "okay?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4664.06,
      "end": 4665.06,
      "text": "Friday Night Connection,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4665.62,
      "end": 4666.56,
      "text": "the Friday Rock Show,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4667.26,
      "end": 4668.78,
      "text": "BBC Radio 1,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4669.24,
      "end": 4669.56,
      "text": "London,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4669.9,
      "end": 4671.4,
      "text": "W1A4WW.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4671.4,
      "end": 4677.18,
      "text": "where it gets a £12 record token",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4677.18,
      "end": 4679.28,
      "text": "and something nice out of our",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4679.28,
      "end": 4680.9,
      "text": "goody drawer. And may I say,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4680.98,
      "end": 4683.12,
      "text": "Annie Bigfoot, you have magnificent handwriting.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4683.84,
      "end": 4688.58,
      "text": "Just coming up to 20 minutes",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 4688.58,
      "end": 4690.28,
      "text": "past 11 o'clock, this is",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4690.28,
      "end": 4692.24,
      "text": "the session version of the current single",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4692.24,
      "end": 4694.14,
      "text": "for Gary Moore, Shapes of Things.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 4694.58,
      "end": 4699.38,
      "text": "For that, from our session by Gary Moore,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5040.0,
      "end": 5165.58,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5165.58,
      "end": 5167.6,
      "text": "the repeat session we're putting out tonight, Shapes of",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5167.6,
      "end": 5169.54,
      "text": "Things, the studio version of his",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5169.54,
      "end": 5172.23,
      "text": "current single. Happy birthday",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5172.23,
      "end": 5174.52,
      "text": "to Lisa Bardsley",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5174.52,
      "end": 5176.02,
      "text": "of Lower Parkston,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5176.36,
      "end": 5177.62,
      "text": "Paul Dorsett.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5177.78,
      "end": 5182.14,
      "text": "wants me to say hello to all John Sykes fanatics everywhere.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5183.87,
      "end": 5185.63,
      "text": "And as Lisa says, see you at the Snakes gig,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5186.33,
      "end": 5187.79,
      "text": "Hammeodian, 2nd of April.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5188.19,
      "end": 5189.07,
      "text": "Enjoy it, me dear.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5190.41,
      "end": 5193.41,
      "text": "Hello, Cookie, Childsie, Sharon and Andrea.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5194.11,
      "end": 5195.98,
      "text": "Over there in Northern Ireland, how are you?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5196.32,
      "end": 5197.12,
      "text": "Hope you're all there.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5197.74,
      "end": 5201.52,
      "text": "Andrea, love very much to meet you again, says Cookie.",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 5221.76,
      "end": 5222.22,
      "text": "Thanks, Spider.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5222.46,
      "end": 5224.1,
      "text": "This is our final one from Palace.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5580.0,
      "end": 5733.13,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 5733.13,
      "end": 5734.11,
      "text": "Commercial rock single.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5734.27,
      "end": 5735.57,
      "text": "It's out on the Capitol record label.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5735.57,
      "end": 5737.13,
      "text": "It is called This Can Be The Right One.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5737.25,
      "end": 5739.95,
      "text": "And before that, our final track from the session by Palace.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5740.33,
      "end": 5741.82,
      "text": "The track was called Cut and Run.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5741.96,
      "end": 5742.66,
      "text": "Excellent session.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5742.76,
      "end": 5743.88,
      "text": "Thank you very much indeed, gentlemen.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5744.54,
      "end": 5746.96,
      "text": "It will, of course, be repeated in the near future.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5747.26,
      "end": 5748.76,
      "text": "Got a nice letter here from Michael Fish,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5749.16,
      "end": 5750.64,
      "text": "who, along with a mate of his called Bernie,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5751.2,
      "end": 5753.72,
      "text": "is doing a bit of that engineering up there in Manchester,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5753.86,
      "end": 5754.58,
      "text": "in Manchester Poly.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5754.66,
      "end": 5756.6,
      "text": "And Michael, like a lot of other people, says,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5756.7,
      "end": 5760.52,
      "text": "will we dig out of the archives a band called As Above and So Below?",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5760.92,
      "end": 5763.74,
      "text": "I'll have a word with the governor next week",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5763.74,
      "end": 5764.72,
      "text": "and see if we can dig it out,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5764.72,
      "end": 5766.56,
      "text": "because it really was a good session and I think",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5766.56,
      "end": 5768.76,
      "text": "was before the sort of",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5768.76,
      "end": 5770.51,
      "text": "current, if you like,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5770.63,
      "end": 5772.61,
      "text": "re-emergence of progressive rock",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5772.61,
      "end": 5774.81,
      "text": "as above so below have broken up",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5774.81,
      "end": 5776.85,
      "text": "to the best of my knowledge. This is a band",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5776.85,
      "end": 5778.53,
      "text": "from Stockholm in Sweden, Oz",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 5778.53,
      "end": 5782.13,
      "text": "Magnificent. That's from our repeat session",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 6120.0,
      "end": 7072.39,
      "text": "[Music]",
      "type": "music"
    },
    {
      "start": 7072.39,
      "end": 7074.27,
      "text": "by Gary Moore. The track was called Empty",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7074.27,
      "end": 7076.35,
      "text": "Rooms and before that you heard Yes",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7076.35,
      "end": 7078.17,
      "text": "from their album Drama. The track was",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7078.17,
      "end": 7080.29,
      "text": "Into the Lens and it was especially for",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7080.29,
      "end": 7082.21,
      "text": "a fellow by the name of Steve who is somewhere",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7082.21,
      "end": 7083.71,
      "text": "but that somewhere is",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7083.71,
      "end": 7086.59,
      "text": "well, not next to the lady that he's affianced to",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7086.59,
      "end": 7088.55,
      "text": "Suki of West Yagland Farm",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7088.55,
      "end": 7090.03,
      "text": "Heartland, Biddeford and Devon",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7090.03,
      "end": 7092.69,
      "text": "Stephen, Suki sends you lots of love",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7092.69,
      "end": 7094.93,
      "text": "and we started that set",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7094.93,
      "end": 7095.91,
      "text": "with a track from an album",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7095.91,
      "end": 7097.77,
      "text": "which is out on the Wave record label",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7097.77,
      "end": 7100.41,
      "text": "it's a Swedish import, the band are called Oz",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7100.41,
      "end": 7103.07,
      "text": "the album is called Fire in the Brain",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7103.07,
      "end": 7104.53,
      "text": "the track was Searchlights",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7104.53,
      "end": 7111.83,
      "text": "and that is it for this edition of the Friday Rock Show",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7111.83,
      "end": 7114.33,
      "text": "next week we have Redding Rock Revisited",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7114.33,
      "end": 7115.85,
      "text": "on the bill, 10 years after",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7115.85,
      "end": 7116.97,
      "text": "and others",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7116.97,
      "end": 7120.58,
      "text": "some. The Friday Rock Show is a",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7120.58,
      "end": 7122.48,
      "text": "Tony Wilson production. Tone has got the bug",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7122.48,
      "end": 7124.28,
      "text": "at the moment. Mr. Wilson, get yourself",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7124.28,
      "end": 7127.02,
      "text": "better. Following the midnight",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7127.02,
      "end": 7128.96,
      "text": "pips you will hear on Medium Wave the News",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7128.96,
      "end": 7131.12,
      "text": "on VHF Radio 2.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7131.7,
      "end": 7135.77,
      "text": "My name is Tommy Vance. On behalf",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7135.77,
      "end": 7137.81,
      "text": "of everybody on the music side of Radio 1,",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7137.89,
      "end": 7139.73,
      "text": "I wish you well. Have yourself an extremely",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7139.73,
      "end": 7141.89,
      "text": "pleasant evening and, well, what's left of it,",
      "source": "TV"
    },
    {
      "start": 7142.01,
      "end": 7143.69,
      "text": "and a good morning as well. Do take care.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7144.77,
      "end": 7146.15,
      "text": "Chin up. Keep a smile on your face.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    },
    {
      "start": 7146.53,
      "end": 7147.49,
      "text": "Good night. God bless.",
      "source": "uncertain"
    }
  ]
}